      'like FAIL_ON_WARNINGS but in case no WARN_LOGFILE is defined Doxygen will not' + #10 +
      'write the warning messages in between other messages but write them at the end' + #10 +
      'of a run, in case a WARN_LOGFILE is defined the warning messages will be' + #10 +
      'besides being in the defined file also be shown at the end of a run, unless' + #10 +
      'the WARN_LOGFILE is defined as - i.e. standard output (stdout) in that case' + #10 +
      'the behavior will remain as with the setting FAIL_ON_WARNINGS.' + #10 +
      'Possible values are: NO, YES, FAIL_ON_WARNINGS and FAIL_ON_WARNINGS_PRINT.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'WARN_FORMAT';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 2;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: '$file:$line: $text'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The WARN_FORMAT tag determines the format of the warning messages that Doxygen' + #10 +
      'can produce. The string should contain the $file, $line, and $text tags, which' + #10 +
      'will be replaced by the file and line number from which the warning originated' + #10 +
      'and the warning text. Optionally the format may contain $version, which will' + #10 +
      'be replaced by the version of the file (if it could be obtained via' + #10 +
      'FILE_VERSION_FILTER)' + #10 +
      'See also: WARN_LINE_FORMAT' + #10 +
      'The default value is: $file:$line: $text.'),
    (Name: 'WARN_LINE_FORMAT';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 2;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: 'at line $line of file $file'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'In the $text part of the WARN_FORMAT command it is possible that a reference' + #10 +
      'to a more specific place is given. To make it easier to jump to this place' + #10 +
      '(outside of Doxygen) the user can define a custom "cut" / "paste" string.' + #10 +
      'Example:' + #10 +
      'WARN_LINE_FORMAT = "''vi $file +$line''"' + #10 +
      'See also: WARN_FORMAT' + #10 +
      'The default value is: at line $line of file $file.'),
    (Name: 'WARN_LOGFILE';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 2;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The WARN_LOGFILE tag can be used to specify a file to which warning and error' + #10 +
      'messages should be written. If left blank the output is written to standard' + #10 +
      'error (stderr). In case the file specified cannot be opened for writing the' + #10 +
      'warning and error messages are written to standard error. When as file - is' + #10 +
      'specified the warning and error messages are written to standard output' + #10 +
      '(stdout).'),
    (Name: 'INPUT';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'filedir'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The INPUT tag is used to specify the files and/or directories that contain' + #10 +
      'documented source files. You may enter file names like myfile.cpp or' + #10 +
      'directories like /usr/src/myproject. Separate the files or directories with' + #10 +
      'spaces. See also FILE_PATTERNS and EXTENSION_MAPPING' + #10 +
      'Note: If this tag is empty the current directory is searched.'),
    (Name: 'INPUT_ENCODING';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: 'UTF-8'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'This tag can be used to specify the character encoding of the source files' + #10 +
      'that DoxyPas reads. The default is UTF-8 and a file that is not valid UTF-8 is' + #10 +
      'read in the ANSI code page of the system (that is how the Delphi sources' + #10 +
      'written before Unicode are), so the tag is needed only when the files are in' + #10 +
      'another encoding: ISO-8859-1, windows-1252, windows-1250, UTF-16... A file' + #10 +
      'that starts with a byte order mark is read in the encoding of the mark,' + #10 +
      'whatever this tag says.' + #10 +
      'See also: INPUT_FILE_ENCODING' + #10 +
      'The default value is: UTF-8.'),
    (Name: 'INPUT_FILE_ENCODING';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The INPUT_FILE_ENCODING tag can be used to specify the character encoding on a' + #10 +
      'per file pattern basis. DoxyPas will compare the file name with each pattern' + #10 +
      'and apply the encoding instead of the default INPUT_ENCODING if there is a' + #10 +
      'match. The character encodings are a list of the form: pattern=encoding (like' + #10 +
      '*.pas=windows-1252).' + #10 +
      'See also: INPUT_ENCODING for further information on supported encodings.'),
    (Name: 'FILE_PATTERNS';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '*.pas|*.dpr|*.dpk|*.pp|*.p|*.lpr|*.dfm|*.fmx';
     Doc: 'If the value of the INPUT tag contains directories, you can use the' + #10 +
      'FILE_PATTERNS tag to specify one or more wildcard patterns (like *.pas and' + #10 +
      '*.dpr) to filter out the source-files in the directories.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'DoxyPas reads Object Pascal only (Delphi and Free Pascal), so the default list' + #10 +
      'has the extensions of those source files. The forms (*.dfm, *.fmx) are only' + #10 +
      'read when PASCAL_PARSE_DFM is set to YES, and the include files (*.inc) are' + #10 +
      'left out: they are read through the units that include them.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'If left blank the following patterns are tested:*.pas, *.dpr, *.dpk, *.pp,' + #10 +
      '*.p, *.lpr, *.dfm and *.fmx.'),
    (Name: 'RECURSIVE';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The RECURSIVE tag can be used to specify whether or not subdirectories should' + #10 +
      'be searched for input files as well.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'EXCLUDE';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'filedir'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The EXCLUDE tag can be used to specify files and/or directories that should be' + #10 +
      'excluded from the INPUT source files. This way you can easily exclude a' + #10 +
      'subdirectory from a directory tree whose root is specified with the INPUT tag.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note that relative paths are relative to the directory from which Doxygen is' + #10 +
      'run.'),
    (Name: 'EXCLUDE_SYMLINKS';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The EXCLUDE_SYMLINKS tag can be used to select whether or not files or' + #10 +
      'directories that are symbolic links (a Unix file system feature) are excluded' + #10 +
      'from the input.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'EXCLUDE_PATTERNS';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '*/__history/*|*/__recovery/*|*/backup/*';
     Doc: 'If the value of the INPUT tag contains directories, you can use the' + #10 +
      'EXCLUDE_PATTERNS tag to specify one or more wildcard patterns to exclude' + #10 +
      'certain files from those directories.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note that the wildcards are matched against the file with absolute path, so to' + #10 +
      'exclude all test directories for example use the pattern */test/*' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'The default list has the folders where Delphi (__history, __recovery) and' + #10 +
      'Lazarus (backup) keep the previous versions of the files.*/__history/*,' + #10 +
      '*/__recovery/* and */backup/*.'),
    (Name: 'EXCLUDE_SYMBOLS';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The EXCLUDE_SYMBOLS tag can be used to specify one or more symbol names' + #10 +
      '(namespaces, classes, functions, etc.) that should be excluded from the' + #10 +
      'output. The symbol name can be a fully qualified name, a word, or if the' + #10 +
      'wildcard * is used, a substring. Examples: ANamespace, AClass,' + #10 +
      'ANamespace::AClass, ANamespace::*Test'),
    (Name: 'EXAMPLE_PATH';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'filedir'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The EXAMPLE_PATH tag can be used to specify one or more files or directories' + #10 +
      'that contain example code fragments that are included (see the \include' + #10 +
      'command).'),
    (Name: 'EXAMPLE_PATTERNS';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '*';
     Doc: 'If the value of the EXAMPLE_PATH tag contains directories, you can use the' + #10 +
      'EXAMPLE_PATTERNS tag to specify one or more wildcard pattern (like *.cpp and' + #10 +
      '*.h) to filter out the source-files in the directories. If left blank all' + #10 +
      'files are included.'),
    (Name: 'EXAMPLE_RECURSIVE';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the EXAMPLE_RECURSIVE tag is set to YES then subdirectories will be' + #10 +
      'searched for input files to be used with the \include or \dontinclude commands' + #10 +
      'irrespective of the value of the RECURSIVE tag.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'IMAGE_PATH';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'filedir'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The IMAGE_PATH tag can be used to specify one or more files or directories' + #10 +
      'that contain images that are to be included in the documentation (see the' + #10 +
      '\image command).'),
    (Name: 'INPUT_FILTER';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The INPUT_FILTER tag can be used to specify a program that Doxygen should' + #10 +
      'invoke to filter for each input file. Doxygen will invoke the filter program' + #10 +
      'by executing (via popen()) the command:' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      '<filter> <input-file>' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'where <filter> is the value of the INPUT_FILTER tag, and <input-file> is the' + #10 +
      'name of an input file. Doxygen will then use the output that the filter' + #10 +
      'program writes to standard output. If FILTER_PATTERNS is specified, this tag' + #10 +
      'will be ignored.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note that the filter must not add or remove lines; it is applied before the' + #10 +
      'code is scanned, but not when the output code is generated. If lines are added' + #10 +
      'or removed, the anchors will not be placed correctly.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note that Doxygen will use the data processed and written to standard output' + #10 +
      'for further processing, therefore nothing else, like debug statements or used' + #10 +
      'commands (so in case of a Windows batch file always use @echo OFF), should be' + #10 +
      'written to standard output.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note that for custom extensions or not directly supported extensions you also' + #10 +
      'need to set EXTENSION_MAPPING for the extension otherwise the files are not' + #10 +
      'properly processed by Doxygen.' + #10 +
      ''),
    (Name: 'FILTER_PATTERNS';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The FILTER_PATTERNS tag can be used to specify filters on a per file pattern' + #10 +
      'basis. Doxygen will compare the file name with each pattern and apply the' + #10 +
      'filter if there is a match. The filters are a list of the form: pattern=filter' + #10 +
      '(like *.cpp=my_cpp_filter). See INPUT_FILTER for further information on how' + #10 +
      'filters are used. If the FILTER_PATTERNS tag is empty or if none of the' + #10 +
      'patterns match the file name, INPUT_FILTER is applied.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note that for custom extensions or not directly supported extensions you also' + #10 +
      'need to set EXTENSION_MAPPING for the extension otherwise the files are not' + #10 +
      'properly processed by Doxygen.' + #10 +
      ''),
    (Name: 'FILTER_SOURCE_FILES';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the FILTER_SOURCE_FILES tag is set to YES, the input filter (if set using' + #10 +
      'INPUT_FILTER) will also be used to filter the input files that are used for' + #10 +
      'producing the source files to browse (i.e. when SOURCE_BROWSER is set to YES).' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'FILTER_SOURCE_PATTERNS';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: 'FILTER_SOURCE_FILES';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The FILTER_SOURCE_PATTERNS tag can be used to specify source filters per file' + #10 +
      'pattern. A pattern will override the setting for FILTER_PATTERN (if any) and' + #10 +
      'it is also possible to disable source filtering for a specific pattern using' + #10 +
      '*.ext= (so without naming a filter).' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag FILTER_SOURCE_FILES is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'USE_MDFILE_AS_MAINPAGE';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the USE_MDFILE_AS_MAINPAGE tag refers to the name of a markdown file that' + #10 +
      'is part of the input, its contents will be placed on the main page' + #10 +
      '(index.html). This can be useful if you have a project on for instance GitHub' + #10 +
      'and want to reuse the introduction page also for the Doxygen output.'),
    (Name: 'IMPLICIT_DIR_DOCS';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 3;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the IMPLICIT_DIR_DOCS tag is set to YES, any README.md file found in' + #10 +
      'sub-directories of the project''s root, is used as the documentation for that' + #10 +
      'sub-directory, except when the README.md starts with a \dir, \page or' + #10 +
      '\mainpage command. If set to NO, the README.md file needs to start with an' + #10 +
      'explicit \dir command in order to be used as directory documentation.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.'),
    (Name: 'SOURCE_BROWSER';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 4;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the SOURCE_BROWSER tag is set to YES then a list of source files will be' + #10 +
      'generated. Documented entities will be cross-referenced with these sources.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note: To get rid of all source code in the generated output, make sure that' + #10 +
      'also VERBATIM_HEADERS is set to NO.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'INLINE_SOURCES';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 4;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'Setting the INLINE_SOURCES tag to YES will include the body of functions,' + #10 +
      'multi-line macros, enums or list initialized variables directly into the' + #10 +
      'documentation.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'STRIP_CODE_COMMENTS';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 4;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'Setting the STRIP_CODE_COMMENTS tag to YES will instruct Doxygen to hide any' + #10 +
      'special comment blocks from generated source code fragments. Normal C, C++ and' + #10 +
      'Fortran comments will always remain visible.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.'),
    (Name: 'REFERENCED_BY_RELATION';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 4;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the REFERENCED_BY_RELATION tag is set to YES then for each documented' + #10 +
      'entity all documented functions referencing it will be listed.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'REFERENCES_RELATION';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 4;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the REFERENCES_RELATION tag is set to YES then for each documented function' + #10 +
      'all documented entities called/used by that function will be listed.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'REFERENCES_LINK_SOURCE';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 4;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the REFERENCES_LINK_SOURCE tag is set to YES and SOURCE_BROWSER tag is set' + #10 +
      'to YES then the hyperlinks from functions in REFERENCES_RELATION and' + #10 +
      'REFERENCED_BY_RELATION lists will link to the source code. Otherwise they will' + #10 +
      'link to the documentation.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.'),
    (Name: 'SOURCE_TOOLTIPS';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 4;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'SOURCE_BROWSER';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If SOURCE_TOOLTIPS is enabled (the default) then hovering a hyperlink in the' + #10 +
      'source code will show a tooltip with additional information such as prototype,' + #10 +
      'brief description and links to the definition and documentation. Since this' + #10 +
      'will make the HTML file larger and loading of large files a bit slower, you' + #10 +
      'can opt to disable this feature.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag SOURCE_BROWSER is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'ALPHABETICAL_INDEX';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 5;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the ALPHABETICAL_INDEX tag is set to YES, an alphabetical index of all' + #10 +
      'compounds will be generated. Enable this if the project contains a lot of' + #10 +
      'classes, structs, unions or interfaces.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.'),
    (Name: 'IGNORE_PREFIX';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 5;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: 'ALPHABETICAL_INDEX';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The IGNORE_PREFIX tag can be used to specify a prefix (or a list of prefixes)' + #10 +
      'that should be ignored while generating the index headers. The IGNORE_PREFIX' + #10 +
      'tag works for classes, function and member names. The entity will be placed in' + #10 +
      'the alphabetical list under the first letter of the entity name that remains' + #10 +
      'after removing the prefix.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag ALPHABETICAL_INDEX is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the GENERATE_HTML tag is set to YES, Doxygen will generate HTML output' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_OUTPUT';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'dir'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: 'html'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_OUTPUT tag is used to specify where the HTML docs will be put. If a' + #10 +
      'relative path is entered the value of OUTPUT_DIRECTORY will be put in front of' + #10 +
      'it.' + #10 +
      'The default directory is: html.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_FILE_EXTENSION';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '.html'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_FILE_EXTENSION tag can be used to specify the file extension for each' + #10 +
      'generated HTML page (for example: .htm, .php, .asp).' + #10 +
      'The default value is: .html.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_HEADER';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_HEADER tag can be used to specify a user-defined HTML header file for' + #10 +
      'each generated HTML page. If the tag is left blank Doxygen will generate a' + #10 +
      'standard header.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'To get valid HTML the header file that includes any scripts and style sheets' + #10 +
      'that Doxygen needs, which is dependent on the configuration options used (e.g.' + #10 +
      'the setting GENERATE_TREEVIEW). It is highly recommended to start with a' + #10 +
      'default header using' + #10 +
      'doxygen -w html new_header.html new_footer.html new_stylesheet.css' + #10 +
      'YourConfigFile' + #10 +
      'and then modify the file new_header.html. See also section "Doxygen usage" for' + #10 +
      'information on how to generate the default header that Doxygen normally uses.' + #10 +
      'Note: The header is subject to change so you typically have to regenerate the' + #10 +
      'default header when upgrading to a newer version of Doxygen. For a description' + #10 +
      'of the possible markers and block names see the documentation.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_FOOTER';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_FOOTER tag can be used to specify a user-defined HTML footer for each' + #10 +
      'generated HTML page. If the tag is left blank Doxygen will generate a standard' + #10 +
      'footer. See HTML_HEADER for more information on how to generate a default' + #10 +
      'footer and what special commands can be used inside the footer. See also' + #10 +
      'section "Doxygen usage" for information on how to generate the default footer' + #10 +
      'that Doxygen normally uses.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_STYLESHEET';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_STYLESHEET tag can be used to specify a user-defined cascading style' + #10 +
      'sheet that is used by each HTML page. It can be used to fine-tune the look of' + #10 +
      'the HTML output. If left blank Doxygen will generate a default style sheet.' + #10 +
      'See also section "Doxygen usage" for information on how to generate the style' + #10 +
      'sheet that Doxygen normally uses.' + #10 +
      'Note: It is recommended to use HTML_EXTRA_STYLESHEET instead of this tag, as' + #10 +
      'it is more robust and this tag (HTML_STYLESHEET) will in the future become' + #10 +
      'obsolete.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_EXTRA_STYLESHEET';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_EXTRA_STYLESHEET tag can be used to specify additional user-defined' + #10 +
      'cascading style sheets that are included after the standard style sheets' + #10 +
      'created by Doxygen. Using this option one can overrule certain style aspects.' + #10 +
      'This is preferred over using HTML_STYLESHEET since it does not replace the' + #10 +
      'standard style sheet and is therefore more robust against future updates.' + #10 +
      'Doxygen will copy the style sheet files to the output directory.' + #10 +
      'Note: The order of the extra style sheet files is of importance (e.g. the last' + #10 +
      'style sheet in the list overrules the setting of the previous ones in the' + #10 +
      'list).' + #10 +
      'Note: Since the styling of scrollbars can currently not be overruled in' + #10 +
      'Webkit/Chromium, the styling will be left out of the default doxygen.css if' + #10 +
      'one or more extra stylesheets have been specified. So if scrollbar' + #10 +
      'customization is desired it has to be added explicitly. For an example see the' + #10 +
      'documentation.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_EXTRA_FILES';
     Kind: okList; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_EXTRA_FILES tag can be used to specify one or more extra images or' + #10 +
      'other source files which should be copied to the HTML output directory. Note' + #10 +
      'that these files will be copied to the base HTML output directory. Use the' + #10 +
      '$relpath^ marker in the HTML_HEADER and/or HTML_FOOTER files to load these' + #10 +
      'files. In the HTML_STYLESHEET file, use the file name only. Also note that the' + #10 +
      'files will be copied as-is; there are no commands or markers available.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_COLORSTYLE';
     Kind: okEnum; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: 'AUTO_LIGHT'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: 'LIGHT|DARK|AUTO_LIGHT|AUTO_DARK|TOGGLE';
     Doc: 'The HTML_COLORSTYLE tag can be used to specify if the generated HTML output' + #10 +
      'should be rendered with a dark or light theme.' + #10 +
      'Possible values are: LIGHT always generates light mode output, DARK always' + #10 +
      'generates dark mode output, AUTO_LIGHT automatically sets the mode according' + #10 +
      'to the user preference, uses light mode if no preference is set (the default),' + #10 +
      'AUTO_DARK automatically sets the mode according to the user preference, uses' + #10 +
      'dark mode if no preference is set and TOGGLE allows a user to switch between' + #10 +
      'light and dark mode via a button.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: AUTO_LIGHT.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_COLORSTYLE_HUE';
     Kind: okInt; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '220'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 359;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_COLORSTYLE_HUE tag controls the color of the HTML output. Doxygen' + #10 +
      'will adjust the colors in the style sheet and background images according to' + #10 +
      'this color. Hue is specified as an angle on a color-wheel, see' + #10 +
      'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hue for more information. For instance the value' + #10 +
      '0 represents red, 60 is yellow, 120 is green, 180 is cyan, 240 is blue, 300' + #10 +
      'purple, and 360 is red again.' + #10 +
      'Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 359, default value: 220.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_COLORSTYLE_SAT';
     Kind: okInt; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '100'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 255;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_COLORSTYLE_SAT tag controls the purity (or saturation) of the colors' + #10 +
      'in the HTML output. For a value of 0 the output will use gray-scales only. A' + #10 +
      'value of 255 will produce the most vivid colors.' + #10 +
      'Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 255, default value: 100.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_COLORSTYLE_GAMMA';
     Kind: okInt; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '80'; MinVal: 40; MaxVal: 240;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HTML_COLORSTYLE_GAMMA tag controls the gamma correction applied to the' + #10 +
      'luminance component of the colors in the HTML output. Values below 100' + #10 +
      'gradually make the output lighter, whereas values above 100 make the output' + #10 +
      'darker. The value divided by 100 is the actual gamma applied, so 80 represents' + #10 +
      'a gamma of 0.8, The value 220 represents a gamma of 2.2, and 100 does not' + #10 +
      'change the gamma.' + #10 +
      'Minimum value: 40, maximum value: 240, default value: 80.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_DYNAMIC_MENUS';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the HTML_DYNAMIC_MENUS tag is set to YES then the generated HTML' + #10 +
      'documentation will contain a main index with vertical navigation menus that' + #10 +
      'are dynamically created via JavaScript. If disabled, the navigation index will' + #10 +
      'consists of multiple levels of tabs that are statically embedded in every HTML' + #10 +
      'page. Disable this option to support browsers that do not have JavaScript,' + #10 +
      'like the Qt help browser.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_DYNAMIC_SECTIONS';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the HTML_DYNAMIC_SECTIONS tag is set to YES then the generated HTML' + #10 +
      'documentation will contain sections that can be hidden and shown after the' + #10 +
      'page has loaded.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_CODE_FOLDING';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the HTML_CODE_FOLDING tag is set to YES then classes and functions can be' + #10 +
      'dynamically folded and expanded in the generated HTML source code.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_COPY_CLIPBOARD';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the HTML_COPY_CLIPBOARD tag is set to YES then Doxygen will show an icon in' + #10 +
      'the top right corner of code and text fragments that allows the user to copy' + #10 +
      'its content to the clipboard. Note this only works if supported by the browser' + #10 +
      'and the web page is served via a secure context (see:' + #10 +
      'https://www.w3.org/TR/secure-contexts/), i.e. using the https: or file:' + #10 +
      'protocol.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_PROJECT_COOKIE';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'Doxygen stores a couple of settings persistently in the browser (via e.g.' + #10 +
      'cookies). By default these settings apply to all HTML pages generated by' + #10 +
      'Doxygen across all projects. The HTML_PROJECT_COOKIE tag can be used to store' + #10 +
      'the settings under a project specific key, such that the user preferences will' + #10 +
      'be stored separately.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_INDEX_NUM_ENTRIES';
     Kind: okInt; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '100'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 9999;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'With HTML_INDEX_NUM_ENTRIES one can control the preferred number of entries' + #10 +
      'shown in the various tree structured indices initially; the user can expand' + #10 +
      'and collapse entries dynamically later on. Doxygen will expand the tree to' + #10 +
      'such a level that at most the specified number of entries are visible (unless' + #10 +
      'a fully collapsed tree already exceeds this amount). So setting the number of' + #10 +
      'entries 1 will produce a full collapsed tree by default. 0 is a special value' + #10 +
      'representing an infinite number of entries and will result in a full expanded' + #10 +
      'tree by default.' + #10 +
      'Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 9999, default value: 100.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'GENERATE_HTMLHELP';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the GENERATE_HTMLHELP tag is set to YES then Doxygen generates three' + #10 +
      'additional HTML index files: index.hhp, index.hhc, and index.hhk. The' + #10 +
      'index.hhp is a project file that can be read by Microsoft''s HTML Help Workshop' + #10 +
      'on Windows. In the beginning of 2021 Microsoft took the original page, with' + #10 +
      'a.o. the download links, offline (the HTML help workshop was already many' + #10 +
      'years in maintenance mode). You can download the HTML help workshop from the' + #10 +
      'web archives at Installation executable (see:' + #10 +
      'http://web.archive.org/web/20160201063255/https://download.microsoft.com/download/0/A/9/0A939EF6-E31C-430F-A3DF-DFAE7960D564/htmlhelp.exe).' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'The HTML Help Workshop contains a compiler that can convert all HTML output' + #10 +
      'generated by Doxygen into a single compiled HTML file (.chm). Compiled HTML' + #10 +
      'files are now used as the Windows 98 help format, and will replace the old' + #10 +
      'Windows help format (.hlp) on all Windows platforms in the future. Compressed' + #10 +
      'HTML files also contain an index, a table of contents, and you can search for' + #10 +
      'words in the documentation. The HTML workshop also contains a viewer for' + #10 +
      'compressed HTML files.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'CHM_FILE';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTMLHELP';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The CHM_FILE tag can be used to specify the file name of the resulting .chm' + #10 +
      'file. You can add a path in front of the file if the result should not be' + #10 +
      'written to the html output directory.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTMLHELP is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HHC_LOCATION';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTMLHELP';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The HHC_LOCATION tag can be used to specify the location (absolute path' + #10 +
      'including file name) of the HTML help compiler (hhc.exe). If non-empty,' + #10 +
      'Doxygen will try to run the HTML help compiler on the generated index.hhp.' + #10 +
      'The file has to be specified with full path.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTMLHELP is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'GENERATE_CHI';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTMLHELP';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The GENERATE_CHI flag controls if a separate .chi index file is generated' + #10 +
      '(YES) or that it should be included in the main .chm file (NO).' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTMLHELP is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'CHM_INDEX_ENCODING';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTMLHELP';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The CHM_INDEX_ENCODING is used to encode HtmlHelp index (hhk), content (hhc)' + #10 +
      'and project file content.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTMLHELP is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'BINARY_TOC';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTMLHELP';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The BINARY_TOC flag controls whether a binary table of contents is generated' + #10 +
      '(YES) or a normal table of contents (NO) in the .chm file. Furthermore it' + #10 +
      'enables the Previous and Next buttons.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTMLHELP is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'TOC_EXPAND';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTMLHELP';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The TOC_EXPAND flag can be set to YES to add extra items for group members to' + #10 +
      'the table of contents of the HTML help documentation and to the tree view.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTMLHELP is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'SITEMAP_URL';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'string'; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The SITEMAP_URL tag is used to specify the full URL of the place where the' + #10 +
      'generated documentation will be placed on the server by the user during the' + #10 +
      'deployment of the documentation. The generated sitemap is called sitemap.xml' + #10 +
      'and placed on the directory specified by HTML_OUTPUT. In case no SITEMAP_URL' + #10 +
      'is specified no sitemap is generated. For information about the sitemap' + #10 +
      'protocol see https://www.sitemaps.org' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'DISABLE_INDEX';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If you want full control over the layout of the generated HTML pages it might' + #10 +
      'be necessary to disable the index and replace it with your own. The' + #10 +
      'DISABLE_INDEX tag can be used to turn on/off the condensed index (tabs) at top' + #10 +
      'of each HTML page. A value of NO enables the index and the value YES disables' + #10 +
      'it. Since the tabs in the index contain the same information as the navigation' + #10 +
      'tree, you can set this option to YES if you also set GENERATE_TREEVIEW to YES.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'GENERATE_TREEVIEW';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The GENERATE_TREEVIEW tag is used to specify whether a tree-like index' + #10 +
      'structure should be generated to display hierarchical information. If the tag' + #10 +
      'value is set to YES, a side panel will be generated containing a tree-like' + #10 +
      'index structure (just like the one that is generated for HTML Help). For this' + #10 +
      'to work a browser that supports JavaScript, DHTML, CSS and frames is required' + #10 +
      '(i.e. any modern browser). Windows users are probably better off using the' + #10 +
      'HTML help feature. Via custom style sheets (see HTML_EXTRA_STYLESHEET) one can' + #10 +
      'further fine tune the look of the index (see "Fine-tuning the output"). As an' + #10 +
      'example, the default style sheet generated by Doxygen has an example that' + #10 +
      'shows how to put an image at the root of the tree instead of the PROJECT_NAME.' + #10 +
      'Since the tree basically has more details information than the tab index, you' + #10 +
      'could consider setting DISABLE_INDEX to YES when enabling this option.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'PAGE_OUTLINE_PANEL';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'When GENERATE_TREEVIEW is set to YES, the PAGE_OUTLINE_PANEL option determines' + #10 +
      'if an additional navigation panel is shown at the right hand side of the' + #10 +
      'screen, displaying an outline of the contents of the main page, similar to' + #10 +
      'e.g. https://developer.android.com/reference If GENERATE_TREEVIEW is set to' + #10 +
      'NO, this option has no effect.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'FULL_SIDEBAR';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'When GENERATE_TREEVIEW is set to YES, the FULL_SIDEBAR option determines if' + #10 +
      'the side bar is limited to only the treeview area (value NO) or if it should' + #10 +
      'extend to the full height of the window (value YES). Setting this to YES gives' + #10 +
      'a layout similar to e.g. https://docs.readthedocs.io with more room for' + #10 +
      'contents, but less room for the project logo, title, and description. If' + #10 +
      'GENERATE_TREEVIEW is set to NO, this option has no effect.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'ENUM_VALUES_PER_LINE';
     Kind: okInt; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '4'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 20;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The ENUM_VALUES_PER_LINE tag can be used to set the number of enum values that' + #10 +
      'Doxygen will group on one line in the generated HTML documentation.' + #10 +
      '' + #10 +
      'Note that a value of 0 will completely suppress the enum values from appearing' + #10 +
      'in the overview section.' + #10 +
      'Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 20, default value: 4.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'SHOW_ENUM_VALUES';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: '';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'When the SHOW_ENUM_VALUES tag is set doxygen will show the specified' + #10 +
      'enumeration values besides the enumeration mnemonics.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.'),
    (Name: 'TREEVIEW_WIDTH';
     Kind: okInt; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '250'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 1500;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the treeview is enabled (see GENERATE_TREEVIEW) then this tag can be used' + #10 +
      'to set the initial width (in pixels) of the frame in which the tree is shown.' + #10 +
      'Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 1500, default value: 250.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'EXT_LINKS_IN_WINDOW';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the EXT_LINKS_IN_WINDOW option is set to YES, Doxygen will open links to' + #10 +
      'external symbols imported via tag files in a separate window.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'OBFUSCATE_EMAILS';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '1'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'If the OBFUSCATE_EMAILS tag is set to YES, Doxygen will obfuscate email' + #10 +
      'addresses.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: YES.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'HTML_FORMULA_FORMAT';
     Kind: okEnum; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: 'png'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: 'png|svg';
     Doc: 'If the HTML_FORMULA_FORMAT option is set to svg, Doxygen will use the pdf2svg' + #10 +
      'tool (see https://github.com/dawbarton/pdf2svg) or inkscape (see' + #10 +
      'https://inkscape.org) to generate formulas as SVG images instead of PNGs for' + #10 +
      'the HTML output. These images will generally look nicer at scaled resolutions.' + #10 +
      'Possible values are: png (the default) and svg (looks nicer but requires the' + #10 +
      'pdf2svg or inkscape tool).' + #10 +
      'The default value is: png.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'FORMULA_FONTSIZE';
     Kind: okInt; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '10'; MinVal: 8; MaxVal: 50;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'Use this tag to change the font size of LaTeX formulas included as images in' + #10 +
      'the HTML documentation. When you change the font size after a successful' + #10 +
      'Doxygen run you need to manually remove any form_*.png images from the HTML' + #10 +
      'output directory to force them to be regenerated.' + #10 +
      'Minimum value: 8, maximum value: 50, default value: 10.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'FORMULA_MACROFILE';
     Kind: okString; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: 'file'; Depends: '';
     Default: ''; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'The FORMULA_MACROFILE can contain LaTeX \newcommand and \renewcommand commands' + #10 +
      'to create new LaTeX commands to be used in formulas as building blocks. See' + #10 +
      'the section "Including formulas" for details.'),
    (Name: 'USE_MATHJAX';
     Kind: okBool; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'GENERATE_HTML';
     Default: '0'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: '';
     Doc: 'Enable the USE_MATHJAX option to render LaTeX formulas using MathJax (see' + #10 +
      'https://www.mathjax.org) which uses client side JavaScript for the rendering' + #10 +
      'instead of using pre-rendered bitmaps. Use this if you do not have LaTeX' + #10 +
      'installed or if you want to formulas look prettier in the HTML output. When' + #10 +
      'enabled you may also need to install MathJax separately and configure the path' + #10 +
      'to it using the MATHJAX_RELPATH option.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: NO.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'MATHJAX_VERSION';
     Kind: okEnum; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'USE_MATHJAX';
     Default: 'MathJax_2'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: 'MathJax_2|MathJax_3|MathJax_4';
     Doc: 'With MATHJAX_VERSION it is possible to specify the MathJax version to be used.' + #10 +
      'Note that the different versions of MathJax have different requirements with' + #10 +
      'regards to the different settings, so it is possible that also other MathJax' + #10 +
      'settings have to be changed when switching between the different MathJax' + #10 +
      'versions.' + #10 +
      'Possible values are: MathJax_2, MathJax_3 and MathJax_4.' + #10 +
      'The default value is: MathJax_2.' + #10 +
      'This tag requires that the tag USE_MATHJAX is set to YES.'),
    (Name: 'MATHJAX_FORMAT';
     Kind: okEnum; OrgKind: okBool; Group: 6;
     Format: ''; Depends: 'USE_MATHJAX';
     Default: 'HTML-CSS'; MinVal: 0; MaxVal: 0;
     Values: 'HTML-CSS|NativeMML|chtml|SVG';
     Doc: 'When MathJax is enabled you can set the default output format to be used for' + #10 +
      'the MathJax output. For more details about the output format see MathJax' + #10 +
      'version 2 (see:' + #10 +
      'https://docs.mathjax.org/en/v2.7/output.html), MathJax version 3 (see:' + #10 +
      'https://docs.mathjax.org/en/v3.2/output/index.html) and MathJax version 4' + #10 +
      '(see:' + #10 +
      'https://docs.mathjax.org/en/v4.0/output/index.htm).' + #10 +
      'Possible values are: HTML-CSS (which is slower, but has the best' + #10 +
      'compatibility. This is the name for Mathjax version 2, for MathJax version 3' + #10 +
